---
import Layout from '../../studio/layouts/Layout.astro';
import { mailto, studio } from '../../apps/registry';

const title = 'Privacy Policy — Tunedot';
const description = 'Privacy policy for Tunedot (com.yanerapps.tunedot), an offline music player for Android by Yaner Apps.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="prose">
    <nav aria-label="Tunedot navigation" class="product-nav">
      <a href="/privacy">Privacy by app</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> Tunedot
    </nav>
    <div class="prose-header">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">Tunedot for Android (<code>com.yanerapps.tunedot</code>)</p>
      <div class="meta">
        <span>Effective: from Tunedot&rsquo;s release on Google Play</span>
        <span>&middot;</span>
        <span>Updated: 18 Nov 2026</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <p><strong>In short:</strong> Tunedot has no ads, no analytics, no crash reporting and no account. The app itself has no internet permission, so it cannot send anything to us or to anyone else.</p>
    </div>

    <p>
      Tunedot is made by Yaner Apps. This policy covers the Tunedot app for Android phones.
    </p>
    <h2>What stays on your phone</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Your music.</strong> Tunedot reads the audio files on your phone to play them. It never changes, moves or deletes a file.</li>
      <li><strong>Your library</strong>: the songs' tags and the covers taken from them, and the folders you chose.</li>
      <li><strong>Playlists, Favorites, the Queue and Places</strong>, where you stopped in each album, playlist, folder and long track.</li>
      <li><strong>Listening history</strong>: play counts and Recently played. Clear listening history in Settings removes them.</li>
      <li><strong>Settings.</strong></li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Uninstalling Tunedot removes everything it stored on your phone. Your music files are not touched.
    </p>
    <h2>Permissions</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Audio files</strong>, to find and play your music. Tunedot does not ask for access to all files.</li>
      <li><strong>Notifications</strong>, for the playback controls. Refusing it never stops playback.</li>
      <li><strong>Foreground service for media playback and keeping the phone awake</strong>, so music keeps playing with the screen off. Both are used only while something plays.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Tunedot does not ask for your location, contacts, camera, microphone or photos, and it never fetches covers, tags or lyrics online.
    </p>
    <h2>Android backup</h2>
    <p>
      Tunedot turns off Android's cloud backup and device-to-device transfer for everything it stores. To move your playlists, Favorites, the Queue, Places, play counts and settings, use Back up in Settings: it writes one file wherever you pick in the system file picker. The file holds no audio and is not encrypted; once it leaves Tunedot, it is yours to protect.
    </p>
    <h2>Notifications and widgets</h2>
    <p>
      The media notification, the lock screen controls and the home screen widgets show the cover, title and artist of what is playing, so anyone who can see your screen can see them. You can hide notification content on the lock screen in Android's settings.
    </p>
    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      Tunedot is not directed at children and collects no personal data from anyone.
    </p>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the new version will be posted at this address with a new date.
    </p>

    <h2>Additional information for the EEA, UK and Switzerland</h2>
    <p>
      This section gives the information required by the EU and UK General Data Protection Regulation and
      the Swiss Federal Act on Data Protection.
    </p>

    <h3>Controller</h3>
    <p>
      The controller for the processing described in this policy is Yaner Yang, publishing as Yaner Apps,
      reachable at <a href={mailto()}>{studio.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>Purposes and legal bases</h3>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Purpose</th>
            <th>Data</th>
            <th>Legal basis</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Answering your emails</td>
            <td>Your email address and your message</td>
            <td>Legitimate interests in responding to you (Art. 6(1)(f)); we delete the correspondence once the matter is closed, and within 12 months at the latest</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      Data that stays on your device is not processed by us at all. You are not required to
      provide any personal data. We make no decisions based solely on automated processing.
    </p>

    <h3>Your rights under the GDPR</h3>
    <p>
      You have the right to access, rectify and erase your personal data, to restrict or object to its
      processing, and to data portability. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data
      protection supervisory authority, in particular in the country where you live or work; in the UK this
      is the Information Commissioner's Office, and in Switzerland the Federal Data Protection and
      Information Commissioner. The section below explains how to exercise these rights.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or port your personal data.
      Since Tunedot keeps your data on your device, you can exercise these rights directly in the app. If you need
      help, write to <a href={mailto()}>{studio.email}</a> and we will respond within 30 days.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Yaner Apps &mdash; <a href={mailto()}>{studio.email}</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
